; BTN-1 (2026-09-19) — THE DROP-OFF BIN. Where the seeker puts the object, and therefore where
; the round ends: the instant the target lands in here the door to the task room bursts open.
;
; AN OPEN-TOP BOX WITH A SENSOR IN IT, and both halves matter. The walls are real static bodies,
; so a prop tossed at it can MISS and roll away, and the seeker can see at a glance whether the
; thing went in — a trigger volume with no box would be an invisible rule. The sensor is an
; Area3D the SERVER reads; clients never decide what is in the bin.
;
; NOTHING IS EVER EJECTED (the packet is explicit). A wrong prop buzzes at the seeker, flashes
; the lamp red for half a second, and stays exactly where it fell. That is the honest version:
; the bin is a place, not a machine with opinions.
;
; WHERE IT IS, AND WHY THERE — MOVED BY HOLD-1 (2026-09-19) WHEN BTN-1 AND SHELF-1 MET.
; Local (−6.2, 0, 0) — world (33.8, 0, 0), because Supermarket.tscn instances this room at
; x = +40. Against the −X end wall, on the room's long midline, in the 2.4 m CROSS-AISLE.
;
; BTN-1 AUTHORED IT AT LOCAL (0, 0, −4) AND THAT WAS RIGHT FOR AN EMPTY ROOM. SHELF-1 then
; dressed the room, and the two are not compatible — neither lane could see the other, and the
; defect only exists in the merged tree:
;   - IT INTERSECTED A SHELF. Aisle 0's bays sit at z = −3.15, 0.50 m deep, so z ∈ [−3.40, −2.90]
;     across x ∈ [−4.6, 4.6]. A 1.4 m bin at z = −4 spans z ∈ [−4.70, −3.30] — 0.10 m INSIDE
;     that bay, and its 0.41 m rim runs straight through the lowest board (0.375–0.425 m).
;   - IT WAS UNREACHABLE IN A STRAIGHT LINE. The dressed room is four bays with 1.6 m walkways
;     between them and NO cross-aisle except at each end (|x| > 4.6). The bin sat in the outer
;     −Z walkway with no crate in it, so every approach crossed a bay.
;   - AND A 1.4 m BIN BLOCKS A 1.6 m WALKWAY. 0.2 m of gap against a 0.72 m capsule is a wall.
;
; THE CROSS-AISLE IS THE ONLY PLACE IN THE DRESSED ROOM THAT ALL FOUR AISLES OPEN ONTO, which is
; both the fix and the better level: the seeker emerges from whichever aisle they searched and
; the bin is there, next to the CONFIRM button on the same end wall. It leaves 0.9 m of clear
; cross-aisle at x ∈ [−5.5, −4.6] to walk past on — against a 0.72 m avatar capsule
; (AvatarProportions: 0.5043 half-width × 0.7138), which is a squeeze and not a block.
;
; CHECKED AGAINST EVERY NEIGHBOUR RATHER THAN BY EYE, which is what BTN-1's own header asked of
; whoever moved it. Bin outer is x ∈ [−6.9, −5.5], z ∈ [−0.7, 0.7], rim y = 0.41:
;   - EndCap_1 (x ∈ [−5.10, −4.60], z ∈ [2.45, 3.85]) — no z overlap.
;   - ConfirmButton (−6.94, 1.15, −3) — 2.3 m in z, and 0.74 m above the rim anyway.
;   - SearchPillar (6, 1, 2.5) — the far end of the room.
;   - SearchSpawn_0 (−4.5, 1.1, 0), the nearest marker — 1.0 m from the bin's +X face, 0.64 m
;     of clearance on the capsule, so nobody spawns inside it.
;   - Run-PlaceTest.ps1's four bots: A places at (0.2, ·, 0) local, 5.7 m away; B stands at
;     Prop_3 and places 5 m off; C walks the z ≈ 2..2.5 walkway to the pillar at (6, ·, 2.5);
;     D walks to the +X wall. None of the four comes near the −X end. Re-run and green, §below.
;   - The −X end wall's inner face is x = −7, so the bin stands 0.1 m off it. Nothing walks there.
;
; 1.4 m SQUARE OUTSIDE, 1.28 m CLEAR INSIDE, and that number has a reason: two 0.44 m crates have
; to be able to sit in it side by side and BOTH pass placement integrity, because the delivery
; smoke puts a wrong prop in first and the real one in after it. At 1.1 m outside they did not
; fit and the second placement was refused DoesNotFitThere — a suite failing on the bin's size
; rather than on the bin's rule.
;
; LOW WALLS (0.35 m) ON PURPOSE. The seeker has to be able to drop a 0.2 m object in from a
; standing position without a throwing minigame; a deep bin would turn the payoff moment into an
; aiming test. The rim is also what keeps a prop that went in from rolling back out.

[node name="DropOffBin" type="Node3D" parent="." groups=["dropoff_bin"]]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, -6.2, 0, 0)
script = ExtResource("3_bin")

